        "Divide both sides by $x$: $x = 9$",
        "So the only solution is 9"
      ],
      "wrong": 1,
      "why": "Dividing by $x$ throws away $x = 0$. Instead: $x^{2} - 9x = 0$, $x(x - 9) = 0$, so $x = 0$ or 9."
    },
    {
      "type": "order",
      "prompt": "Solve $(x - 3)^{2} = 16$. Put the steps in order.",
      "items": [
        "Take the square root of both sides: $x - 3 = \\pm 4$",
        "Split it: $x - 3 = 4$ or $x - 3 = -4$",
        "Solve: $x = 7$ or $x = -1$"
      ],
      "why": "Don't forget the negative root."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "Solve $x^{2} - 4x + 1 = 0$.",
      "choices": [
        "$2 \\pm \\sqrt{3}$",
        "$4 \\pm \\sqrt{3}$",
        "$2 \\pm \\sqrt{5}$",
        "$-2 \\pm \\sqrt{3}$"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "why": "$x = (4 \\pm \\sqrt{16 - 4}) / 2 = (4 \\pm 2\\sqrt{3}) / 2 = 2 \\pm \\sqrt{3}$.",
      "rematch": true
    }
  ],
  "keys": [
